course: dictionary
lesson: 9204
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word sol is a good example. «A day on Mars, called a sol, is about 24 hours 40 minutes» tells you that sol is a day on Mars, because the sentence is about how long a day lasts.
explain: Look at the words around the word. Sol with a capital S is a name for the Sun, and sol can also be a music note, a kind of liquid, or money. Ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then test it by putting your meaning into the sentence in place of the word.
explain: Some words come from other languages too. In French, sol means floor or ground, so «sur le sol» means on the ground. In Spanish and Portuguese, sol means sun. These are not English meanings, so in an English text, check the English meanings first.
fact: Sol is a name for our Sun, from Latin.
fact: A sol is one day on Mars, about 24 hours 40 minutes, so it is a little longer than an Earth day.
fact: Sol, also written so or soh, is the fifth note of the do-re-mi scale.
fact: A sol is a liquid with tiny solid bits spread through it.
fact: The sol is the money of Peru.
exercise: «A day on Mars, called a sol, is about 24 hours 40 minutes.» What is a sol here? | A note in a song | A kind of money | *A day on Mars | The Sun
exercise: «The choir sang do, re, mi, fa, sol, la, ti, do.» What is sol in this sentence? | *A note in the do-re-mi scale | The name of our Sun | A kind of money | A tiny solid bit in a liquid
exercise: «On sol 100 the rover found a rock.» What does sol mean here? | *A day on Mars | A kind of liquid | The money of Peru | The Sun
test: In a French lesson, the teacher says «Le livre est sur le sol.» What does sol mean? | The Sun | The money of Peru | *Floor or ground | A music note
test: «Sol rose over the city, and the spaceship landed.» What does sol mean in this sentence? | *Our Sun | A sol of Mars | A liquid with tiny bits | The money of Peru
exam: «In Lima, the shopkeeper took the sol.» What does sol mean? | A day on Mars | The name of a music note | Floor or ground | *The money of Peru
